what if kokoshibo fought against the  other upper moons in blood battles would  he be able to prove that he is the  strongest or is there someone who can  defeat him and take the title for  himself today we will be going through  all of kokoshibo's battles against the  upper moons and we even have a special  showdown at the end which you definitely  don't want to miss even as a hashira  kokoshiba was already extremely strong  as he had access to the transparent  world and selfless state he was the  second strongest ashira and could easily  kill scores of demons his breathing  technique moon breathing is the second  strongest breathing technique in the  entire series second only to sun  breathing as a human kokoshiba was  extremely jealous of his younger  brother's skill and strength he wanted  to surpass his brother and become the  strongest and he would do anything to  make that happen this deep hatred and  jealousy were what pushed him to become  a demon after his transformation he  quickly became immensely powerful and  occupied the position of upper moon 1.  if kokoshibo ever fought against lower  moons it would be a child's play for him  the lower moons are just too weak  compared with their upper moon  counterparts his mere presence would  send shivers down the spines of all the  lower moons as they would easily be able  to ascertain the vast difference in  strength just to paint a more vivid  picture the upper moons remained  unchanged for over a century they've  gone on to kill scores of ashira the  highest ranked demon slayers for  instance the upper moon 6 dhaki and  gyutara have killed 7 and 14 hashiras  and they are the weakest upper moons so  we can only imagine how many hashiras  kokoshiba must have killed meanwhile the  ranks of the lower moons constantly  change because they are always killed by  any hashira who crossed his paths with  them this fact angered muzon and made  him wipe out all the lower moons now the  real blood battles start let's see how  kokoshiba would fare against the upper  moon 6 daki and  as we all know is a weakling the only  reason she is an upper moon is because  of the special privilege muzon gave  gyutaro to also let his sister be an  upper moon with him daki would perform  terribly against kokushibo even though  she has managed to kill seven hashiras  in her lifetime kukushipa would still  kill her in one fell swoop this is  because most of the hasheras she's  killed can be attributed to the help of  her brother in fact when they were  decapitated by tondro in the anime  gyutero revealed that daki would have  been killed several times had he not  rescued her again this goes to show just  how weak she is there's just no way she  can hold her own in a battle against the  strongest upper moon in existence  kokoshibo as for gyotoro he may be able  to hold his ground for some time given  his agility and speed his poisons would  obviously have no effect on kokushibo  even combined both daki and gyotro can't  defeat kokoshibo they're the weakest  upper moons for a reason but would  kokoshipo be capable of slicing off both  of their heads at the same time this  could be quite bothersome even for the  great kokoshibo ultimately he would be  able to decapitate both of them at the  same time since his moon breathing  techniques are capable of sending  multiple attacks simultaneously after  kokoshipo finishes with daki and kyotoro  gyoko will be next in the line kyoko is  strong no doubt he was able to overwhelm  the miss tishira muichiro the first time  they engaged each other this feat is  really impressive considering that  moichiro is a child prodigy and one of  the strongest hashiras in the series  although gyoko had the advantage at the  beginning of the fight he quickly lost  once muichiro awakened his demon slayer  mark fast forward a few months later to  the infinity castle arc moichiro gets  the beating of a lifetime from kokushibo  even with his demon slayer mark awakened  in fact the battle was more of bullying  than an actual fight as kokushiba was  just toying with him and at the same  time effortlessly avoiding his attacks  let's take a logical look at this series  of events marked moichiro defeated gyoko  meanwhile the same marked moyichiro got  destroyed by kokoshibo with this it's  obvious that gyouka would lose in a  battle against kokushibo only three more  challenges are left and the next one is  hantengu antengu would most likely cause  the most headache for kokoshibo compared  to all the demons discussed so far  ultimately kokoshiba would win because  the difference in raw strength and power  between them is very significant but how  long would it take kokoshibo to end the  battle that'll probably depend on how  fast he is able to kill hantengo's  clones since that's one of the latter's  most powerful abilities being able to  create clones of himself each time he is  beheaded huntangu's strongest form  zohakuten is also incredibly strong as  he was capable of using it to battle  mitsuri even with her demon slayer mark  awakened he would probably be able to  stand against kokushibo without dying  immediately in this form but in the end  he would only be buying time and  focusing solely on defense this however  will not save him from the impending  doom that awaits him and at the end of  the day he will still be killed and  there's nothing he can do to avoid it  finally the battle that many fans wanted  to see in the anime but never happened  akaza vs kokushibo akaza is incredibly  strong perhaps just as much as he's  rebellious ideally this battle should be  different and more interesting as this  is the realm of the top three strongest  demons akasa is a martial artist who has  reached the peak of its physical  abilities his immense strength was  witnessed in his battle against rangoku  he basically kept playing with the flame  pillar until he killed him only getting  in slight trouble due to the sun rising  he also battled against giu and tangero  at the same time and he was able to  overpower both of them even though gu  activated his demon slayer mark it's  also important to mention that he and  kokoshibo are the only demons besides  muzon who became immune to decapitation  by nichiren swords with this the only  way to kill them would be to battle them  long enough for the sun to rise another  aspect of akaza's immense strength is  his ability to sense the fighting spirit  of his opponents this bolsters his  offensive and defensive capabilities and  essentially makes him invincible  kokoshibo on the other hand has been  capable of concealing his fighting  spirit ever since he was a human this is  because he gained access to the  transparent world and selfless state as  a hashira so even back then akaza would  find it incredibly difficult to sense  his fighting spirit it's crazy to think  that human kokoshibo already possesses  one of akaza's major weaknesses and that  the latter would probably lose a battle  against him even in his human form  essentially human kokoshibo is  comparable to akaza this means that  demon upper rank 1 kokoshibo would be on  an entirely different level to a kaza  and that he would easily be able to  defeat him let's for instance strip  kokoshibo of his ability to conceal his  presence he would still be capable of  defeating akaza with moon breathing the  second most powerful breathing technique  but he wouldn't accomplish this feat  without a few injuries injuries that'll  literally heal within seconds while  akaza remains dead we will soon cover  the ultimate showdown between kokushibo  and upper moons but before that we still  have one more upper moon to cover the  cult leader doma domo would definitely  be a challenging foe for kokoshibo we  don't know much about the extent of  doma's strength but he's the second  strongest demon in the ranks of the  upper moons and that says a lot how  would he fare in a bout against  kokushibo since we don't know much about  the extent of his strength let's take a  look at some of his feats domo was the  upper moon 5 when he turned daki and  gyotoro into demons thus it's safe to  say that he swiftly ascended into the  position of upper moon 2 since according  to what muzon said the upper moon ranks  have remained unchanged for the past  century this shows that he likely  surpassed some of the already existing  upper moons in terms of strength and  power thus getting him promoted to the  rank of upper moon 2. also he defeated  shinobu a hashira of the demon slayer  core with relative ease after which he  basically toyed with inusuki and canal  in the ensuing combat this shows that he  would prove a pretty troublesome  opponent for kokoshibo another testament  to doma's strength is that he was not  afraid of akaza's attacks and he  continuously irritated him it's sad  however that the full extent of his  power was not revealed the only time he  was about to get serious in battle was  when shinobu's poison began to affect  him but by that time it was too late as  he was already extremely weakened from  the effects of the poison overall the  fact that he is upper rank 2 says a lot  but despite all of his power kokoshibo  still remains the big boss of the upper  moons and he would still emerge  victorious in a battle against doma with  mid-difficulty  and now we are getting to the final act  the ultimate showdown doma and akaza vs  kokushibo despite being the strongest of  all the demons it'll be very tough for  kokoshibo to make it out of this battle  alive firstly it took three of the  strongest ashiras yome sunemi moichiro  plus genya to defeat kokoshipo split  into two there's no way these teams can  defeat doma and akaza in separate  battles even if they choose not to split  up there's no way this team of demons  players can defeat both doma and akaza  if they teamed up and fought side by  side at the same time yet they managed  to defeat kokoshibo akaza is already a  formidable foe and doma is even more  formidable hence as a tag team assuming  they would get along they would  definitely be able to defeat the upper  moon 1 demon the only entity capable of  defeating this duo would be the demon  king himself muzon and of course the  great yorichi tsugikuni check out this  video where we explained what would  happen if ran goku accepted akasa's  offer to transform trust me it's an  excellent video

